{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>One who keeps a commandment knows no evil thing</b> — for nothing will come upon him in abundance." "<b>And the time and judgment the heart of the wise knows.</b> Some interpret עת in this place as though it means wisdom, and they cite as parallels לעות את יעף, דבר ביד איש עתי, יודעי העתים, יודעי בינה לעתים. This is not correct, for the meaning of לעות את יעף is to set him a time, namely יעיר בבוקר בבקר בבקר; and איש עתי means one who is ready to go at that time and will not delay; or its meaning is one whose practice is to go at every time of year to the wilderness mentioned, its sense being like רגיל; and יודעי בינה לעתים — the Rabbis of blessed memory already explained that they were calculators of intercalation of years, and יודעי העתים are men of the constellations. Another interpretation: שומר מצוה — he does not wish to know an evil thing; and the matter of עת ומשפט is joined to the verse after it."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {1 "The phrase יעיר בבוקר בבקר בבקר is obscure as transmitted, possibly corrupt or a cross-reference to a verse like Isaiah 50:4; rendered hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:26.639310640Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}